    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d548">

                <pb facs="0717" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg625"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/8434</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-11T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3055. For Crosby [from Treasury]:</p>
                <p>Your No. 33 for Treasury. Regarding matter of tonnage and whether it can be
                    allocated for transport of troops you will please state that that can be taken
                    up in future when we are faced with practical execution of plan. Please urge
                    concurrence in principle on part of both Governments and state that political
                    situation in China will be much improved by an evidence on part of Allies to
                    allow her cooperation even if practical difficulties actually prevent it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
